MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Aur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Aur_m01_001: Make sure to prepare well. You depart for the\nIsle of Sorrows on {SetColor=Gold}{DateTime=Month} {DateTime=Day}{SetColor=Default}. 
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Aur_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Aur_m03_001: Today's the day you depart for the Isle of Sorrows.\nAre you prepared for your journey?
MID_LGA_1KAI_c06_Aur_m03: <BLN>Today's the day...
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Aur_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Aur_m02_001: You're doing admirably in the Heroic Games, Cai.\nBut I still have to say that I worry about you.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Aur_m02_002: Please be careful, and don't push yourself too far.\nI ask the same of Centurio too.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Aur_m02_003: How are you getting along with Centurio?\nHe's quite adorable.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Aur_m02_004: Yes, Castor and Centurio both look somewhat\nolder now in appearance, yet...
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Aur_m02_005: compared to my own age, they're still quite young.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Aur_m02_006: Yes, there was a rather large age gap between us, as\nhusband and wife...
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Aur_m02_007: You see, I was born in the year 553. That means this\nyear I'll be...896? Yes, 896.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Aur_m02_008: But my age is nobody else's business, is it? Cai, you\nmust never forget that you are half of my blood.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Aur_m02_009: You may well live for five hundred years, do\nyou understand?
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Aur_m02_010: Cai, I hope you know happiness in those years.
MID_LGA_1KAI_c06_Aur_m02: <BLN>You leave on {SetColor=Gold}{DateTime=Month} {DateTime=Day}{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Tia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Tia_m01_001: Cai, look! There's something painted on that wall!
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Tia_m01_002: Do you think it was painted during the time of the\nkingdom of Damascar? Let's take a closer look!
MID_LGA_1KAI_c06_Tia_m01: <BLN>Cai, look at that!
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Tia_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Tia_m02_001: I'll never forget the sight of Ahm Lu as long as I live.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Tia_m02_002: This is what a country looks like once it's destroyed.
MID_LGA_1KAI_c06_Tia_m02: <BLN>I'll never forget...
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Pet_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Pet_m01_001: I've had the feeling for a little bit that we're\nbeing watched.
MID_LGA_1KAI_c06_Pet_m01: <BLN>Is it just in my head?
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Hur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Hur_m01_001: No one else is here—and I think that's been the\ncase for a long time.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Hur_m01_002: Still, I figure we've got good odds of finding risen\ndead here.
MID_LGA_1KAI_c06_Hur_m01: <BLN>Let's stay on our guard.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Cen_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Cen_m01_001: It's as if the forest swallowed the city.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Cen_m01_002: In the long years since the nation's destruction, the\nforces of nature have taken over.
MID_LGA_1KAI_c06_Cen_m01: <BLN>A great and terrible thing...
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Tia_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Tia_m04_001: Your mom said that she had an idea about the\ntrue nature of Drake's treasures.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Tia_m04_002: What do you think she meant?
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Tia_m04_003: Let's go to the Isle of Sorrows as soon as\nyou're ready!
MID_LGA_1KAI_c06_Tia_m04: <BLN>I'm just so curious...
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Pet_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Pet_m03_001: I can't believe I'm doing a favor for a god. It's kind of\nnerve-racking, really.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Pet_m03_002: And what's this Isle of Sorrows about, anyway?\nWhat the heck kind of place is it?
MID_LGA_1KAI_c06_Pet_m03: <BLN>Sounds like a strange place...
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Cas_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Cas_m01_001: Hey, Cai. I've been hearing stories from Gabriel.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Cas_m01_002: Sounds like you're doing well in the Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Cas_m01_003: That's my boy. I'm proud of you.
MID_LGA_1KAI_c06_Cas_m01: <BLN>That's my boy.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Cen_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Cen_m02_001: I never weighed kindness less, but I always weighed\nloyalty more...
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Cen_m02_002: Oh! Cai. My apologies.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Cen_m02_003: I was just remembering a poem I read years ago.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Cen_m02_004: <NCA>Think about it.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Cen_m02_005: <NCB>Say you don't understand.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Cen_m02_006: <ACA>You grasped the meaning right away, didn't you?\nI'd expect nothing less of you.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Cen_m02_007: <ACB>Haha... That's the way of the world, I suppose. It\ntook me many years to understand it myself.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Cen_m02_008: The more years we acquire, the more we understand\ndeep meanings in passages we used to skip over.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Cen_m02_009: The most important thing of all, perhaps, is that you\nlive life in such a way that you have no regrets.
MID_LGA_1KAI_c06_Cen_m02: <BLN>I always weighed loyalty more...
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Hur_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Hur_m02_001: What I know about our destination all comes\nfrom books.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Hur_m02_002: The Isle of Sorrows is just off the coast of Cybele.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Hur_m02_003: And Cybele's within spitting distance of Callisto's\nprimary temple of Aurora.
MID_LGV_1KAI_c06_Hur_m02_004: As for the lands in that area... *sigh*
MID_LGA_1KAI_c06_Hur_m02: <BLN>The Isle of Sorrows...